    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`POST /api/owners`).\n\n**The change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. **Read the header** \u2014 the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` signature only carries the request body, so I pull the optional `Idempotency-Key` header from the current request via `RequestContextHolder` in a new `idempotencyKey()` helper (returns `null` when absent/blank).\n\n2. **Replay on a seen key** \u2014 at the very start of `addOwner`, before any validation/duplicate checks run, if the key has been seen the controller fetches the originally created owner and returns it with **200 OK** (rather than falling through to the normal path, which would 409 on the duplicate).\n\n3. **Record on create** \u2014 after a successful `saveOwner`, the key \u2192 new owner id is stored in a `ConcurrentHashMap` field, so a later repeat replays it.\n\nThe `coreIdempotentRepeat` acceptance test passes: first create returns 2xx (201), the repeat with the same key returns 200, and both yield the same owner id. All other tests remain green.\n\nA note on the storage choice: the mapping lives in an in-process `ConcurrentHashMap` on the singleton controller bean, which satisfies the spec and the test. If you later want this to survive restarts or work across multiple instances, it should be promoted to a persistent/shared store (e.g. a small JPA entity or a cache) \u2014 happy to do that if that's the intended scope.",
