    "probe_text": "Here is the exact, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. The active persistence profile is `spring-data-jpa` (per `application.properties`).\n\n## Phase A \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (before the controller runs)\n\n`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` is validated by the framework. Failures throw `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** (`ExceptionControllerAdvice`). Constraints on `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n\n1. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n2. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`, `@Size(1..30)`\n3. `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)` (optional)\n4. `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n5. `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n6. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n7. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n8. `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n9. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n10. `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` (LocalDate)\n11. `title` \u2014 `@Size(1..10)`\n\nNo custom validators, no `@InitBinder`, no validation groups.\n\n## Phase B \u2014 Controller body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`), in order\n\n12. **Idempotency replay check** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior create whose owner still exists, return that owner with **200 OK** (short-circuit, no new create).\n13. **Normalize address** \u2014 canonicalize `addressLine1/2` and `address`, compose back into `address`.\n14. **Reject blank fields** \u2014 require non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, address, `city`, `telephone`; else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n15. **Validate postcode against city/region** \u2014 `PostcodeValidator`; else \u2192 **400** (`postcode`).\n16. **Normalize telephone** \u2014 to E.164; invalid \u2192 **400** (`telephone`).\n17. **Normalize email** \u2014 trim/lowercase, syntax check, reject disposable domains; invalid \u2192 **400** (`email`). (Skipped if email absent.)\n18. **Compute householdId** \u2014 from `lastName` + `postcode`.\n19. **Read `sharesHousehold` flag.**\n20. **Reject duplicate identity** \u2014 compares normalized telephone key against all non-deleted owners; collision \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n21. **Reject household duplicate** \u2014 if not opting into sharing and the household already exists \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` \u2192 **409**.\n22. **Reject city at capacity** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in that city (case-insensitive) \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n23. **Reject future registration date** \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 **400** (`registrationDate`).\n24. **Compute effective registration date** \u2014 supplied date or today, rolled forward to next business day.\n25. **Count owners registered that day.**\n26. **Reject daily registration limit** \u2014 \u2265 100 that day \u2192 `OwnerDailyRegistrationLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Phase C \u2014 Entity assembly (side-effects on the new entity)\n\n27. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity.**\n28. `setRegistrationDate(...)` \u2014 the adjusted business-day date.\n29. `setHouseholdId(...)`.\n30. `setNamesakeCount(...)` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n31. `setBulkSignupWarning(...)` \u2014 true if that day's count > 80.\n32. `setHouseholdSize(...)` \u2014 household member count + 1.\n33. `markPossibleDuplicate(...)` \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n## Phase D \u2014 Persist (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n\n34. **Assign `customerCode`** (new owners only) \u2014 derive from region/telephone/lastName, then de-duplicate by suffixing `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 against existing codes.\n35. **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** \u2014 Spring Data `em.persist`. On persist, Hibernate **re-runs Bean Validation on the `Owner` entity** (`@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName/address/city, telephone `@Pattern` E.164, `@Email`). No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/entity listeners exist.\n\n## Phase E \u2014 Post-save side-effects\n\n36. **Record idempotency key \u2192 owner id** in the in-memory map.\n37. **Map entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`** (derives membership number/level, check digit, fiscal year, salutation, etc. \u2014 response-only, not stored).\n38. **AUDIT log line** \u2014 SLF4J `\"AUDIT\"` logger emits id/customerCode/registrationDate/membershipLevel/membershipNumber.\n39. **Set `Location` header** and return **201 CREATED**.\n\nNotes worth flagging: there is **no** event publishing, email/notification sending, or password encoding in this flow. All uniqueness checks (identity, household, customer code) are done in-application against the full owner list \u2014 there are no DB unique constraints enforcing them."
